### 2. Aggregate Design Guidelines

```typescript
// Design principles
const aggregateDesignPrinciples = {
    // Protect invariants
    protectInvariants: 'All state changes go through aggregate root',

    // Small aggregates
    smallAggregates: 'Reference other aggregates by ID, not object',

    // Transaction boundary
    transactionBoundary: 'One aggregate per transaction',

    // Event-driven
    eventSourcing: 'Consider event sourcing for complex aggregates'
};

// Good aggregate boundary
class OrderAggregate {
    // Order items are part of order aggregate
    // Customer is referenced by ID
    // Product is referenced by ID
}

// Bad aggregate boundary
class OrderAggregate {
    // Including customer, product details
    // Makes aggregate too large
}
```

